      "text": "Caño Negro Wildlife Refuge"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:4b5ff9b4a37f43cc",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "d21d4c250c846bf673c2e7fa854d6ebc8247e449fc58c93c32d7ca2bcf58b64f",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-worker-mw96kqoe-lg4q4klwz6",
        "model": "GPT-6"
      },
      "text": "After breakfast, take a boat tour of Caño Negro and the Río Frío.\n\nThe trip begins in Los Chiles, a small town about 4 km from the Nicaraguan border.\n\nThe river is part of the Caño Negro Wildlife Refuge, a designated Ramsar wetland.\n\nLook out for a variety of birds along the river, including anhingas, herons and cormorants.\n\nYou may also see howler monkeys, spider monkeys, white-faced capuchins and three-toed sloths.\n\nCaimans, basilisks known as “Jesus Christ lizards”, and turtles also live in the area.\n\nMost of the day is spent on the water, so this is a good option if you want to watch wildlife without a long walk.\n\nReturn to the Arenal area after lunch.\n\nBreakfast and lunch are included."
    },
